course: dictionary
lesson: 15218
title: Separated: apart or sorted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Separated means apart, not together any more. It is the past form of separate, which means to move things or people apart. «The twins were separated at the park gate when the crowd pushed.» They are no longer standing side by side, so separated tells you they were moved apart.
explain: Separated can also mean sorted into groups. «The teacher separated the red counters from the blue ones.» Nothing is lost or in danger here. The counters are just put into two piles. Ask yourself: are things apart, or sorted? The rest of the sentence tells you which.
explain: Small words next to separated give clues. «Sam got separated from his dad in the shop» means they were apart, because from points away from someone. «The apples were separated into three equal groups» means they were sorted, because into shows where the apples ended up.
explain: Some sentences are about families. «When my parents separated, they decided to live in two homes.» Separated here means they chose to live apart. This happens to many families, and it is never a child's fault.
fact: Separate is the base word; separated is the past form.
fact: «Separated» means apart, not together any more.
fact: «Separated» can also mean sorted into groups.
fact: If you get separated in a shop or crowd, stay where you are, or go to a shop worker, a police officer or a parent with children, and say your name.
fact: Mixtures can be separated by sieving, filtering, evaporating or with a magnet.
exercise: «The little dog got separated from its owner at the beach.» What does separated mean here? | Very happy | Sorted into groups | *Apart, not together any more | Washed clean
exercise: «The teacher separated the 24 pencils into four equal groups.» What does separated mean here? | Broken in two | Lost forever | *Sorted into groups | Ran away fast
exercise: «If you get separated in a shop, what should you do?» Choose the safest answer. | Run out of the shop as fast as you can | Hide behind the shelves | *Stay where you are and find a shop worker | Walk home alone
test: «Mum and Dad are separated, but both of them love me very much.» What does separated tell you? | They are going on holiday together | They are very angry with each other | They have just got married | *They have decided to live apart
test: «We separated the sand from the water using a sieve.» Which method is this? | *Sieving | Using a magnet | Freezing | Heating
exam: «The coins were separated by value, so all the pennies were in one pile.» What does separated mean here? | Stuck together | Hidden | Lost | *Sorted into groups
